WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.299
The challenge. Choosing the right school, at the right time, for a growing family is a complex and daunting decision.

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:12.739
House prices are high, costs keep rising, and future income is less certain than it used to be.

00:00:13.189 --> 00:00:20.660
John: Our biggest issue was trying to balance everything at once: our mortgage, the costs of moving to a bigger house with a larger mortgage,

00:00:20.660 --> 00:00:24.367
while still giving our children the best education we could afford.

00:00:24.817 --> 00:00:28.487
Jane: Every time we changed one thing, we had to rework all the others.

00:00:28.937 --> 00:00:34.455
Meet John and Jane. They solved it with the Interactive Planning Board in Easy School Fees Planner.

00:00:34.455 --> 00:00:39.305
It puts school fees, your next home and your household money on one page, year by year.

00:00:40.805 --> 00:00:48.512
Setting up takes a few minutes. Add each parent's pay, your children's years of birth, the schools you're considering, and the homes you might buy.

00:00:48.512 --> 00:00:55.013
The planner reads each school's published fees, and works out take-home pay, stamp duty, the larger loan and the repayments.

00:00:55.463 --> 00:01:01.073
John: We added two schools we were weighing up, and the bigger house we had our eye on. That was all it needed.

00:01:02.573 --> 00:01:12.067
Everything you entered now sits on one board. There's a row for each child's school years, one for your home, and one for work and savings, with the money position underneath.

00:01:12.517 --> 00:01:22.437
Now the hard part becomes simple. Drag the home purchase to a different year, and the larger mortgage, the repayments and the school fees you can still afford all update straight away.

00:01:22.887 --> 00:01:25.148
John: Let's see what happens if we buy a year later.

00:01:25.598 --> 00:01:31.763
Real life brings other costs too. Add an expense in seconds: a name, a type, an amount and a year.

00:01:32.213 --> 00:01:36.523
Jane: We added a new car in 2030. Thirty thousand dollars. That was it.

00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:41.383
Move a child's school years, or stretch a rental. Add a work break, or a windfall.

00:01:41.383 --> 00:01:47.085
Years where the money doesn't stretch are flagged, so you can see exactly which choice causes the squeeze.

00:01:47.535 --> 00:01:50.820
Jane: It used to be a spreadsheet nightmare. Now it's a few drags.

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.995
Jane: We didn't need to understand the maths. We just moved things around until the plan stopped squeezing us.

00:01:58.445 --> 00:02:05.591
John: It turned one huge, tangled problem into a few simple choices: which school, which year, which house, and what we could afford.

00:02:06.041 --> 00:02:09.369
Try as many what-ifs as you like before you commit to any of them.

00:02:10.869 --> 00:02:15.500
The Reports page turns your chosen plan into clear charts and tables you can print.

00:02:15.500 --> 00:02:25.376
Your information stays yours: when you save to the cloud, your plan is encrypted in your own browser, so no one else can read it. The built-in assistant never sees your numbers.

00:02:26.876 --> 00:02:34.812
The planner gives general information, not personal financial advice, so speak with a licensed professional before making big decisions.

00:02:35.262 --> 00:02:36.969
Jane: Now we can plan with confidence.

00:02:37.419 --> 00:02:40.981
John: The school fees and the bigger home, in one plan we can afford.

00:02:41.431 --> 00:02:47.490
Look up your school's fees free, then start your seven-day trial at easyschoolfeesplanner.com.au.
